    "summary": "Deleted the graph store's temporary reader declaration function and its _mayReadLiveStore flag from src/db/graph/store.ts (the MCP server's call was removed in t9); assertMayOpen now admits only a process that declared itself the owner, and resetLiveStoreDeclarationsForTests forgets only that. The store-child helper loses its 'declare-reader' command and gains a default case that answers an unknown command with an error. Reader cases turned into refusal cases: live-store-owner.test.ts (only the owner declaration opens the live path; the store module exports no declaration but declareLiveStoreOwner), live-store-refusal.test.ts (a new third-process test: beside the owner, a process with no declaration is refused LmdbStoreNotOwnerError and holds no descriptor before or after; the old reader command is refused), live-vector-store-owner.test.ts (no declaration but the owner's exists; the live vector store is refused). The 'exactly two places' scan is replaced by one that fails on any occurrence under src/ (all file types it may appear in, tests included) and builds the name from pieces. New ac6 integration test src/mcp/__tests__/mcp-process-refused.test.ts: a child process with HOME in a temporary directory starts the real MCP server via runInsrcMcpStdio (as src/bin/insrc-mcp.ts does), then tries getGraphStore() and getLanceConn() on its live paths: both refused (LmdbStoreNotOwnerError, LanceStoreNotOwnerError / lance-not-owner) and nothing created. Mutations: making the MCP startup declare the owner fails the ac6 test; re-adding the name in a comment fails the scan. Full sweep under Node v22.23.2 recorded in docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/sweeps.md (row t11): 6649 tests, only the 9 known failures/cancellations, nothing newly failing.",
